#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""hearth-accounts: your online accounts, set up once in Settings > Accounts and
used by every app (almanac's mail, calendars and contacts, grove's servers and
Google documents, …).

  hearth-accounts serve                  the D-Bus service (started on demand)
  hearth-accounts list                   -> {"ok", "accounts": [...], "registrations": {...}}
  hearth-accounts save JSON|-           add or change an account -> {"ok", "id"} ("-": the JSON is in
                                         $HEARTH_ACCOUNTS_INPUT, so a password never shows in a command line)
  hearth-accounts remove ID
  hearth-accounts registration PROVIDER JSON   the app registration (client ID…) for a provider
  hearth-accounts sign-in PROVIDER [ID]  browser sign-in, waits -> {"ok", "id", "email"} or {"ok": false, "error"}
                                         (nextcloud: ID is the server address)
  hearth-accounts load-registration PROVIDER FILE   a downloaded client file (Google's client_secret_….json)
  hearth-accounts watch                  prints {"changed": true} each time the accounts change
  hearth-accounts code CODE              the code Yahoo/AOL show (or the whole address)
  hearth-accounts cancel                 stop a sign-in that is waiting
  hearth-accounts token ID PURPOSE       an access token (for testing)
  hearth-accounts test ID                try the account (mail: log in to IMAP/SMTP; server: reach it)
  hearth-accounts presets                the mail providers Settings offers, with their servers
  hearth-accounts discover EMAIL         find a mail address's servers (Thunderbird's database)

Everything but `serve` prints one JSON line.

D-Bus: io.github.benwbooth.Accounts at /io/github/benwbooth/Accounts,
interface io.github.benwbooth.Accounts1 (JSON strings in and out):
  List() -> s                    accounts, no secrets
  Password(s id) -> s
  AccessToken(s id, s purpose) -> s   {"token", "expires_in", "email"}; purpose is
                                 mail | calendar | contacts | drive (files the app
                                 made) | files (read all files) | sync (read and
                                 change every file: canopy's Google Drive sync)
      errors io.github.benwbooth.Accounts1.SignedOut (the provider ended the
      sign-in, e.g. Google's 7 days in Testing: sign in again), .NotAllowed (the
      account wasn't allowed that: sign in again and tick it), .Failed
  Save(s json) -> s id           inline "password" and grants[].refresh_token go to
                                 the keyring; the same account (kind + address, or
                                 server) is merged rather than added twice
  Remove(s id)
  Registrations() -> s, SaveRegistration(s provider, s json)
  SignIn(s provider, s id) -> s session   then signal SignInDone(s session, s result)
  SubmitCode(s code), CancelSignIn()
  OpenSettings(s id) -> b        Settings > Accounts (false without hearth)
  signal Changed()

Accounts live in ~/.config/hearth/accounts.json (no secrets); passwords and
refresh tokens in the Secret Service (secret-tool, application=hearth-accounts
account=<id> key=password|refresh:<grant>).

Tests: HEARTH_ACCOUNTS_BROWSER=CMD opens sign-in pages with CMD instead of
xdg-open; HEARTH_ACCOUNTS_DIR=DIR keeps accounts.json there, and secrets in
DIR/secrets.json instead of the keyring; HEARTH_ACCOUNTS_TEST_BASE=URL adds a
"test" provider whose sign-in pages are at URL/auth and URL/token.
"""
